    'Revenue growth and projection: enter the previous and current period revenue and the period length. You get growth, the annualised and monthly compound rates and the doubling time, then a projection for as many periods as you like at the measured rate or one you choose, with an optimistic and conservative band.',
    'Customer retention and churn: enter customers at the start and end of the period and the new customers added. You get the retention and churn rates, their annualised versions, average customer lifetime, the customers needed just to stand still, and, with a revenue-per-customer figure, what the churn costs.',
